# reject-delegation-ungranted-delegator — the empty-set corner of no-amplification
# (§6): a delegator holding no grant over a kind at a gate has the empty risk set
# there, so ANY grant to its delegate at that gate amplifies -> ill-formed at
# apply. A delegate is never granted where its delegator is not. Both actors are
# declared, the chain is a single acyclic link, and no grade is declared: only
# the no-amplification rule can reject.
actor boss
actor sub on-behalf-of boss
gate g risk low grant sub[deploy:low]
cord g -> master
